      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: The `value_` Token holds a `std::string_view` which may point to `shortened_value_`.\n\n`LiteralNode` is unique among AST nodes because it can own the string memory that its `Token` points to (this happens when `shortened_value_` is populated in `ShortenTarget()`).\n\nIf you just copy `value_` here, the new `LiteralNode`\u0027s token will hold a `std::string_view` pointing to the original `LiteralNode`\u0027s `shortened_value_` string buffer. If the original node is destroyed, the token inside the cloned node will become a dangling pointer.\n\nTo fix this, you should also copy `shortened_value_` and update the token to point to the new string if it\u0027s not empty:\n\n```cpp\n  auto node \u003d std::make_unique\u003cLiteralNode\u003e(value_);\n  if (!shortened_value_.empty()) {\n    node-\u003eshortened_value_ \u003d shortened_value_;\n    node-\u003evalue_ \u003d Token(value_.location(), value_.type(), node-\u003eshortened_value_);\n  }\n  return node;\n```",
